  "details": "A prewarmed system should simulate only one loop, not an arbitrary number.\n\nBasically, it should behave like in 2019 and every previous version we had to this day. You know.\n\nDemonstration video: https://files.catbox.moe/z2jkyq.mp4\n\nNote: initially P90 fires off all particles, reaching the preset limit, unable to spawn any more. That should not happen, and instead the system should behave similar to the later seen M4.\n\nSystems on M4/SCAR-L use non-prewarmed setups, systems on Negev & P90 prewarm loops.\n\nSamples: avtr_20c6be99-9208-4b77-82b8-b617558c78ec, avtr_cfb9970f-0fac-49f0-823c-b18b55cc2ee2, avtr_2a4c8fbd-a66c-4061-8db6-8a7cd32af12b (one seen in the video).",
